That's where we disagree. I think the generation of infinite puddings
is fun or many people. I like it because it breaks the normal rules of
the game in an interesting way,and allows for some truly reamrkable,
extreme situations to arise. I think the ability to abuse the game is
also desirable. It's not like you could pud-farm and pretend you
hadn't, or save-scum and pretend you hadn't, or claim a conduct you
hadn't earned (well, no more than it's possible to post YAAP when you
haven't ascended, anyway). My problem is that this exploit comes at
relatively little risk, and that there is an opportunity here to give
pudding farming the potential for even more strange, interesting
situations than we currently have.

I also think it's a shame to take something away from the game when
with a little more work (OK, considerably more work), something new
can be added instead.

